    editorial: "Let `ways[i][j]` be the number of paths to cell `(i, j)`. It equals `ways[i-1][j] + ways[i][j-1]` with `ways[0][*] = ways[*][0] = 1`. Rolling the rows into one array gives O(m*n) time and O(n) space. (A closed form `C(m+n-2, m-1)` also exists, but computing it modulo a prime needs modular inverses; the DP avoids that.)",
